    <string name="pocket_usb_help_title">USB-C streaming setup</string>
    <string name="pocket_usb_help_sub">One-time steps on the handheld and the PC</string>
    <string name="pocket_usb_help_body">Streaming over the cable needs no Wi-Fi and no internet. The cable becomes a private network between the handheld and your PC.\n\nON THE PC (once)\n1. Install Apollo (or Sunshine) and make sure it is running.\n2. Download the pc-setup folder from the Artemis Pocket GitHub page and double-click ArtemisPocket-USB-Setup.bat. It opens the firewall for the USB network and stops Windows from using the handheld for internet.\n\nON THE RETROID (once)\n3. Settings → About device → tap Build number 7 times.\n4. Settings → System → Developer options → Default USB configuration → USB tethering.\n\nEVERY TIME\n5. Open Artemis Pocket and plug the cable into the PC. It finds the PC on its own. The first time, pair with the PIN in Apollo\'s web page.\n\nTips: use a USB 3 port and cable. The handheld charges from the PC while you play, but more slowly than from a wall charger.</string>

